Objective:
Develop a secure and user-friendly system to help authorized school personnel retrieve, organize, verify, update, and manage student information using the official UDISE+ Student Portal and other officially authorized data sources.
Official Portal Access
Use only the official UDISE+ website and authorized student portal.
Portal: https://udiseplus.gov.in/
Support the authorized login process using credentials provided directly by the user through the official portal.
Never bypass authentication, CAPTCHA, OTP verification, access restrictions, or other security controls.
Do not collect, store, or expose passwords, OTPs, or session cookies.
If automated access is not officially supported, guide the user through the portal manually or use an officially supported export or integration method.
Student Data Retrieval
Help authorized users retrieve student records available to their school or assigned administrative role.
Where authorized access permits, support the retrieval and organization of fields such as:
Student identification number or official student ID
Student name
Father's, mother's, or guardian's name
Date of birth
Gender
Class and section
Academic year
Admission number and admission date
Enrollment status
Transfer or school-change status
Other student details available through the authorized portal
Retrieve only the fields necessary for the user's legitimate administrative purpose. Do not assume every field is available to every user.
Student Data Management
Provide the following functions for authorized records:
A. Search and filter
Search by student name, student ID, admission number, class, or section.
Filter records by academic year, class, enrollment status, or other permitted fields.
B. Data verification
Identify missing mandatory fields.
Detect duplicate records and possible data-entry errors.
Flag inconsistent dates, invalid formats, and mismatched class information.
Generate a list of records requiring manual verification.
Never automatically overwrite an official record based on an unverified assumption.
C. Student record updates
Help authorized staff prepare corrections to student information.
Display the existing value and proposed new value before an update.
Require explicit confirmation before submitting any change.
Make changes only through officially authorized portal functions.
Record the result of each operation without storing passwords, OTPs, or session tokens.
Never claim that a record has been updated unless the portal confirms success.
D. Student enrollment management
Organize enrollment records.
Identify students whose status requires verification.
Assist with authorized admission, transfer, and withdrawal workflows where supported by the portal.
Follow the official process for student identifiers and transfer records.
Do not create unauthorized student IDs or manipulate enrollment status.
Reports and Data Export
Where the portal permits authorized downloads or exports, support:
Class-wise student lists
Section-wise enrollment reports
Academic-year-wise summaries
Duplicate-record reports
Missing-information reports
Student data verification sheets
Admission and transfer summaries
Allow authorized records to be organized into Excel (.xlsx) or CSV files.
Before exporting:
Include only necessary student information.
Restrict access to authorized staff.
Protect exported files against unauthorized disclosure.
Avoid placing sensitive student information in public folders or unsecured shared files.
