Voice Search for Student Names
Add a microphone button beside the student search bar.
When the user taps the microphone:
Activate the Android speech recognition feature.
Display the message "Listening... Speak the student's name."
Convert the user's speech into text.
Automatically enter the recognized name into the student search field.
Search the authorized student database for matching records.
Display matching students in a list.
Allow the user to select a student to view their permitted details.
Example:
User says: "Search for Ayaan Ahmad."
The app enters: "Ayaan Ahmad"
The app searches the available student records.
Matching results appear on the screen.
Voice Typing for Student Names
Add a microphone icon beside the student name input field in the Add Student and Edit Student screens.
When the user taps the microphone:
Start speech recognition.
Recognize the spoken student name.
Insert the recognized text into the student name field.
Allow the user to review and correct the spelling.
Save the name only after the user confirms the entry and submits the form.
Example:
The user speaks "Mohammad Arif" and the app inserts "Mohammad Arif" into the name field.
The user can correct the recognized text before saving it.
Support Indian Names and Languages
Configure speech recognition to support languages relevant to the school's users, including:
English (India)
Hindi
Urdu, where supported by the selected speech recognition service
Other Indian languages supported by the device
Allow the user to select the recognition language.
Preserve the original recognized script. For example, do not automatically convert Urdu or Hindi names into English or another script.
Support common variations in the pronunciation of Indian names.
Search Matching
Implement intelligent search for student names.
Search should support:
Exact name matches
Partial name matches
First-name searches
Full-name searches
Minor differences in spaces and capitalization
Optional fuzzy matching for possible spelling differences
Display possible matches instead of automatically selecting a student when multiple records have similar names.
Never change an official student record merely because a voice search returned a possible match.
Android Development Requirements
If the existing application is built with Kotlin, implement the feature using Kotlin. If it uses Java, follow the existing Java architecture.
Use Android's "SpeechRecognizer" API where supported, or another appropriate speech recognition service.
Requirements:
Request microphone permission at runtime.
Check whether speech recognition is available.
Handle microphone denial and recognition errors.
Display listening, processing, success, and failure states.
Provide a button to stop listening.
Release the speech recognizer when it is no longer needed.
Avoid recording or storing audio unnecessarily.
Provide manual keyboard entry as a fallback.
Handle network connectivity requirements for the chosen recognition service.
Follow the Android lifecycle and accessibility guidelines.
User Interface
Create a simple, modern interface with:
A student search field
A microphone button
A language selection option
A clear-search button
A voice recognition status indicator
A list of matching students
An editable student name field
A confirmation button before saving changes
Suggested interaction:
"Tap Microphone → Speak Student Name → Convert Speech to Text → Review Text → Search Records"
For new or edited student records:
"Tap Microphone → Speak Name → Insert Name → Verify Spelling → Save"
UDISE+ Integration
The voice feature must work only with student records the logged-in user is authorized to access.
If the app uses imported UDISE+ data, search those authorized records.
If the app connects to the official UDISE+ Student Portal, use only officially supported APIs, integrations, or permitted portal workflows.
Do not bypass login, CAPTCHA, OTP, access controls, or other security restrictions. Do not assume that a public API exists.
Voice search should retrieve records, not automatically modify official student information.
Expected Deliverables
Provide:
Complete implementation compatible with the existing Android project.
Kotlin or Java source code, as appropriate.
Required Android manifest permissions.
Microphone permission handling.
Speech recognition implementation.
Student name search functionality.
Voice-based name entry functionality.
Language selection and error handling.
UI integration instructions.
Testing instructions for different accents and supported languages.
Before writing the code, inspect the existing project structure and identify the current student search screen, student form, database, and programming language. Integrate the feature into the existing application rather than unnecessarily rebuilding the entire app.
Final objective: Enable school staff to find student records and enter student names by speaking into an Android phone, while allowing them to verify the recognized names before saving or modifying records.

